---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Flag from '../components/Flag.astro';
import DaeroLogo from '../components/DaeroLogo.astro';
import Certifications from '../components/Certifications.astro';
import ProjectPreviews from '../components/ProjectPreviews.astro';
import LogoCards from '../components/LogoCards.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About | Enricco Gemha"
	description="Software engineer from São Paulo, now at Brown. How I got here, and what I’m working on."
>
	<div class="wrapper wrapper-narrow stack gap-12">
		<header class="intro">
			<div class="stack gap-4">
				<h1>About</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					I’m a <span class="nowrap"><Flag country="br" label="Brazilian" /> software</span> engineer living in the US. This is how I got here,
					and what I’m working on now.
				</p>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/assets/portrait.jpg"
				alt="Enricco Gemha, in a navy suit, photographed outdoors in front of evergreen trees."
				width="867"
				height="1200"
				decoding="async"
			/>
		</header>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="how">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="how">How I got here</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					My first code was for my family’s medical accounting office, where I worked in
					high school. Most of the job was paperwork done by hand, so I taught myself
					Python to automate some of it. Then I went to <a href="https://www.insper.edu.br/" rel="noopener" data-preview="school-insper">Insper</a> in São Paulo to pursue a
					B.Sc. in Computer Engineering.
				</p>
				<p>
					Outside class, I was on Insper Dynamics, the student team that built two
					generations of a <a href="/work/robocup/" data-preview="robocup">search-and-rescue robot</a>. Our robots won Best in Class for
					Sensing at RoboCup 2022 in <span class="nowrap">Bangkok <Flag country="th" label="Thailand" /></span>. In early 2023 I became
					president of the college’s robotics and AI club, and that July we won Best in
					Class for Exploration, the autonomous mapping test, at RoboCup 2023 in
					<span class="nowrap">Bordeaux <Flag country="fr" label="France" /></span>. For my capstone I did multi-cloud security for
					<a href="/work/pinpag-capstone/" data-preview="pinpag-capstone">PinPag</a>, a Brazilian payments company, on their live platform.
				</p>
				<p>
					I also studied away from Insper twice. In the summer of 2024 I was a visiting
					student at <a href="https://www.stanford.edu/" rel="noopener" data-preview="school-stanford">Stanford</a>, where I took courses in High-Performance
					Computing and Entrepreneurship and interviewed
					<a href="https://hennessy.stanford.edu/biography" rel="noopener">John L. Hennessy</a> for 30 minutes. He was Stanford’s
					president from 2000 to 2016 and shared the 2017 Turing Award with David
					Patterson. Then, in the spring of 2025, I did an exchange program at
					<a href="https://www.olin.edu/" rel="noopener" data-preview="school-olin">Olin</a> and <a href="https://www.babson.edu/" rel="noopener" data-preview="school-babson">Babson</a>, outside Boston. During
					that semester I started <a href="/work/opengiving/" data-preview="opengiving">OpenGiving</a> with two American
					friends. It’s a marketplace where part of every sale goes to a fundraising
					campaign. I wrote all of its code, and I’ve been on leave from it since I started
					at Brown.
				</p>
				<p>
					In September 2025 I joined <DaeroLogo href="/work/zeropunch/" preview="zeropunch" />, a Boston startup that
					makes software for construction crews, as its first engineering hire. The first
					version of their iOS app, their main product, already existed. I worked on it for
					ten months, and in February 2026 I started rewriting it from scratch, which
					taught me a lot about UX in mobile apps. I also supported the web, backend and
					cloud work. I left in July 2026.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="now">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="now">What I’m doing now</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					I’m pursuing an M.Sc. in Innovation Management and Entrepreneurship at
					<a href="https://www.brown.edu/" rel="noopener" data-preview="school-brown">Brown</a>, and
					I finish in May 2027.
				</p>
				<p>
					But I’m still building my technical skills. This term I’m taking Systems Security
					at <a href="https://www.harvard.edu/" rel="noopener" data-preview="school-harvard">Harvard University</a> (due to Brown offering cross-registration), and I’m
					studying for the CompTIA Security+ certification.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="tools">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="tools">Tools I reach for</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					<strong>Languages.</strong> Swift, Python, TypeScript, Go, Kotlin, C and C++.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Building.</strong> SwiftUI and WidgetKit, FastAPI, Next.js and Astro,
					Jetpack Compose, PostgreSQL with Prisma, GraphQL, Stripe Connect and PayPal.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Running it.</strong> AWS, Railway, Vercel, GitHub Actions,
					OpenTelemetry and Grafana.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Security.</strong> Semgrep in CI, Wazuh, ModSecurity, and secret
					scanning as a required check.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="certifications">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="certifications">Certifications</h2>
			<Certifications />
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="elsewhere">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="elsewhere">Elsewhere</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					I speak Portuguese and English natively, Spanish well enough to work in, and a
					little Swedish. Outside Brazil and the US, I’ve lived in
					<span class="nowrap">Stockholm <Flag country="se" label="Sweden" /></span> and <span class="nowrap">Madrid <Flag country="es" label="Spain" /></span>, for two
					months each.
				</p>
				<p>
					In my free time, I play pickup soccer whenever I can find a game, or you’ll see
					me playing <a href="https://magic.wizards.com/en" rel="noopener" data-preview="game-magic">Magic: The Gathering</a> or retro games (yes, I love my
					<a href="https://www.nintendo.com/en-gb/Hardware/Nintendo-History/Game-Boy-Advance/Game-Boy-Advance-627139.html" rel="noopener" data-preview="game-gba">GBA</a>!).
				</p>
				<p>
					Write to me at <a href="mailto:me@enriccogemha.dev">me@enriccogemha.dev</a>,
					or find me on <a href="https://github.com/G3mha" rel="me noopener">GitHub</a>
					and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/enriccogemha" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
	<ProjectPreviews ids={['robocup', 'pinpag-capstone', 'opengiving', 'zeropunch']} />
	<LogoCards ids={['school-insper', 'school-stanford', 'school-olin', 'school-babson', 'school-brown', 'school-harvard', 'game-magic', 'game-gba']} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.lede {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		color: var(--ink);
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}

	.intro img {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 15rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	@media (min-width: 42em) {
		.intro {
			flex-direction: row;
			align-items: flex-start;
			justify-content: space-between;
			gap: 3rem;
		}

		/* The portrait stays deliberately small. It is here so a recruiter can put a
		   face to the name, not so it competes with the first paragraph. */
		.intro img {
			flex: none;
			width: 13rem;
		}
	}
</style>
